  "body": "## What changed\n- New decision file `docs/decisions/1896-thread-pass-ends.md`. It records why the laid flank passes keep their present ends. This is the second \"Done means\" choice of #1896.\n- The pin `every_pass_runs_to_the_posted_end_z_inside_the_root_pass` keeps its assertion. Its comment now names the decision.\n- No production code changed.\n\n## Cause\nA control that runs G76 ends every flank pass at D. The kernel lays each flank pass as whole half-turns, shifted by its flank offset. Thus a shallower pass ends short of D by `(k - depth) * tan(a/2)`.\n\n## Why the present ends stay\n- The kernel refuses a flank angle wider than the insert's half-angle. Thus the control's extra run-out stays inside the root pass's V at D. It is never deeper than the root pass and never passes D toward the chuck.\n- G32 and G33 passes cut exactly the laid passes. The lathe stock simulation refuses helical passes by name, so no simulated stock differs.\n- A partial helical arc to D ends off the meridian plane. The holder law, the rapid law, both lathe posts (`threadHalfTurn`) and the two thread verdicts read every thread arc as a meridian or antipodal half-turn. To change all of them is a large change to the safety surface for a P7 gain. The decision file lists each part.\n\n## Tests\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test lathe_post_g76_sources`: 3 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test turning_thread_infeed -- plans_that_cannot_cut_refuse_by_name flank_infeed_shifts_each_pass_along_its_flank`: 2 passed. These pin the half-angle refusal that the containment proof uses.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (1 step).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No new pin and no mutation check: this PR changes no behaviour.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The partial-arc design was read in the code, not built. The earlier worker's held pin (`mkinney:issue/1896-thread-pass-ends`, commit 145dcc86) fails on main by design. This decision supersedes it.\n\n## Overlaps\nNone. The open draft #468 changes the thread pass loop, but this PR does not touch it.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1896\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
